WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Self-attention.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:06.067
This is the heart of the transformer, and the classic whiteboard question.

3
00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:10.367
Each token's vector is projected three different ways.

4
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.033
A query says what this token is looking for.

5
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:15.733
A key says what this token can be found by.

6
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.622
And a value is what it hands over if chosen.

7
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:22.033
Keeping keys and values separate is the subtle brilliance.

8
00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:25.433
Here is the whole recipe in one line.

9
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:30.300
Dot products between queries and keys give a score for every pair of tokens.

10
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.233
We divide by root d, so scores stay in a sensible range.

11
00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:39.400
Softmax turns scores into weights, and the output is the weighted sum of the values.

12
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.300
Decoders add one more rule, the causal mask.

13
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.841
Each row is a query.

14
00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:47.633
It may only look at keys at or before itself.

15
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:54.133
Every future score is set to minus infinity before softmax, which makes its weight exactly zero.

16
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:57.100
Here it is in about five lines.

17
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.600
We project the inputs into queries, keys and values.

18
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.567
Then score every pair and scale.

19
00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:05.533
Next we mask the future with minus infinity.

20
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:08.133
Finally softmax, and mix the values.

21
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.133
Two payoffs make this worth knowing.

22
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:17.200
First, causal attention in NumPy is a literal interview question for AI engineer roles.

23
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.600
Second, if you change a future token, earlier outputs never change.

24
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:28.100
That is exactly why the KV cache works: no recomputing thousands of tokens for every new word.

25
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.042
A classic mistake is forgetting the scale.

26
00:01:32.042 --> 00:01:35.567
Large dot products saturate softmax and gradients die.

27
00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:38.767
The fix is simple: divide by the square root of d.

28
00:01:39.967 --> 00:01:40.700
Let's recap.

29
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.467
Queries, keys and values: what to look for, how to be found, and what to give.

30
00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:50.767
Softmax of Q K transpose over root d, times V, is the whole recipe.

31
00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.967
The causal mask hides the future.

32
00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:56.711
So past outputs stay fixed and the KV cache works.

33
00:01:56.711 --> 00:01:58.433
Next up: cross-attention.
